// Personal pattern library / custom functions.
//
// Load with :StrudelLoadPrelude (after :StrudelConnect) - once per session,
// or again any time you edit this file.
//
// IMPORTANT: assign to globalThis, not `const`/`let`. Each :StrudelEval
// (and each StrudelLoadPrelude) runs as its own separate, isolated
// function scope, so a plain `const` here would NOT be visible from
// test.strudel or any other pattern file - only globalThis persists
// across those separate eval() calls.

globalThis.kick4 = (bank) => s("bd*4").bank(bank);

globalThis.riser = (pat) => pat.iter(4).slow(2);

globalThis.arange = (a, b) => Array.from({length: b - a + 1}, (_, i) => a + i);

globalThis.registerControls = (...names) => names.forEach(n => { globalThis[n] = registerControl(n)[n]; });

registerControls('f0ratio', 'f1ratio', 'modInd0', 'modInd1', 'att', 'rel');

// Strudel's evaluate() always expects the last expression to be a Pattern
// (its REPL model treats every eval as "this is what's now playing") - a
// file of nothing but assignments ends in an implicit `undefined`, which it
// rejects with "got 'undefined' instead of pattern". `silence` is a real,
// empty Pattern that satisfies the check without making any sound - keep
// this as the last line whenever you add more to this file.
silence
